		<title type="html"><![CDATA[New MD9600 Beta version 2024 10 18]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4497&amp;p=33549#p33549"><![CDATA[
A new MD9600 Beta is available<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/MD9600/Firmware/5851decfc027fb6c8b84771536290b6eaf1b6ce1" class="postlink">downloads/MD9600/Firmware/5851decfc027f ... 6eaf1b6ce1</a><br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/MD9600/Firmware/Latest" class="postlink">downloads/MD9600/Firmware/Latest</a><br><br>Changes in this version<br><br>* On the Channel Details screen, the repeater Latitude and Longitude can be entered and also the "Use location" setting, can be set to Yes/No.<br>Note. the Use location is called "Location" because "Use location" won't fit on the screen<br>* GPS NMEA output is not disabled during Tx, like it is on other supported radios, becuase the MD9600 can transmit and also output NMEA data at the same time.<br>* Power to the GPS module is turned off when the power button is pressed to turn the radio off. <br>Note. The MD9600 is never completely off. Pressing the power button actually puts the radio into standby, as the MD9600 does not have any hardware to actually disconnect its power supply.<br>* Prevent Roaming channels re-sorting when a scan is ended.<br>* Updates to the Italian language translation<br><br><br>Thanks to Daniel F1RMB for his work on these changes and enhancements, and to IZ2EIB  for the Italian language translation<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri Oct 18, 2024 5:53 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
